  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $3?$\n\nI. $935\\,784$\n\nII. $7\\,391\\,123$\n\nIII. $12\\,144\\,801$",
  "worked_solution": "A number is divisible by $3$ if the sum of its digits is divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $935\\,784$ is\n\n$$\n9+3+5+7+8+4=36,\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $3.$ So, $935\\,784$ is divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $7\\,391\\,123$ is\n\n$$\n7+3+9+1+1+2+3=26,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $3.$ So, $7\\,391\\,123$ is *not* divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $12\\,144\\,801$ is\n\n$$\n1+2+1+4+4+8+0+1=21,\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $3.$ So,  $12\\,144\\,801$ is divisible by $3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
